{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Block still life test passes!\n\n## Red -- Test 8: should preserve block still life unchanged\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: Compiles Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Test passes (block pattern is already handled by reproduction + survival) Correct\n**Result**: Test already passes — 2×2 block correctly preserved\n\nTest already passes -- no new failure to fix. Skipping green/refactor.\n\n## Red -- Test 9: Blinker from vertical to horizontal (gen 0 → gen 1)\n\nVertical blinker: `[(0,0), (0,1), (0,2)]` — three cells in a vertical line at x=0, y=0,1,2.\nExpected: `[(-1,1), (0,1), (1,1)]` — three cells in a horizontal line at y=1, x=-1,0,1.\n\nLet me verify: each `(0,0)` cell has neighbor `(0,1)` only → 1 neighbor → dies. `(0,2)` has `(0,1)` → 1 neighbor → dies. `(0,1)` has `(0,0)` and `(0,2)` — 2 neighbors → survives. Dead cells `(-1,1)` and `(1,1)` each have `(0,0)`, `(0,1)`, `(0,2)` → wait, do they? `(-1,1)` neighbors: `(0,0)` (dx=1,dy=-1 ✓), `(0,1)` (dx=1,dy=0 ✓), `(0,2)` (dx=1,dy=1 ✓) = 3! So `(-1,1)` revives. Similarly `(1,1)` revives with 3 neighbors. \n\nThis test should pass with the current implementation since vertical blinker is symmetric to horizontal (which we already handle).\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01addcdeba26435ebc286ce4","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it(\"should transform blinker from vertical to horizontal (gen 0 → gen 1)\", () => {\n    // Vertical blinker: (0,0), (0,1), (0,2). Expected horizontal: (-1,1), (0,1), (1,1)\n    const result = nextGeneration([[0, 0], [0, 1], [0, 2]]);\n    expect(result).toContainEqual([-1, 1]);\n    expect(result).toContainEqual([0, 1]);\n    expect(result).toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n    expect(result).toHaveLength(3);\n  });","oldText":"  it.todo(\"should transform blinker from vertical to horizontal (gen 0 → gen 1)\");"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_11