derpopulation: each has 1 neighbor → both die) — Example from Rule 1\n4. **Survival — cell with 2 neighbors lives** (Rule 2, simple 2-neighbor case)\n5. **Survival — cell with 3 neighbors lives** (Rule 2, 3-neighbor case — shown in spec as center cell with 3 live neighbors)\n6. **Overpopulation — cell with more than 3 neighbors dies** (Rule 3 — center cell with 4 neighbors dies)\n7. **Reproduction — dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive** (Rule 4)\n8. **Block — still life pattern remains unchanged** (integration: 2×2 block)\n9. **Blinker — oscillator pattern (gen 0 → gen 1)** (integration: vertical → horizontal)\n10. **Blinker — oscillator returns (gen 1 → gen 2)** (integration: horizontal → vertical, verifying revers"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4873fe3935b5434d8bb93213","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_11-54-49_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/game-of-life.spec.ts","content":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"should return empty for empty input\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill a single cell (underpopulation, 0 neighbors)\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill two cells each with 1 neighbor (Rule 1 underpopulation example)\");\n  it.todo(\"should keep cell alive with 2 live neighbors (Rule 2 survival)\");\n  it.todo(\"should keep cell alive with 3 live neighbors (Rule 2 survival)\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill cell with more than 3 neighbors (Rule 3 overpopulation example)\");\n  it.todo(\"should revive dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors (Rule 4 reproduction example)\");\n  it.todo(\"should preserve block still life unchanged\");\n  it.todo(\"should transform blinker from vertical to horizontal (gen 0 → gen 1)\");\n  it.todo(\"should transform blinker from horizontal back to vertical (gen 1 → gen 2)\");\n});"}}],"api":"openai-completions